        "original_id": "5bd41f59-1a2e-5635-8ac1-2bd3d2072571",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Caldera de Taburiente National Park, Teide National Park, La Palma, Tenerife, Canary Islands, Spain\n- Concepts: geological features, national parks, plant distribution, elevation\n- Species: Echium wildpretii subsp. trichosiphon, Adenocarpus viscosus\n- Protected areas: Corona Forestal Nature Park, Reserva Especial de las Palomas\n\nFacts:\n- Caldera de Taburiente National Park is a large geological feature on the island of La Palma in the Canary Islands, Spain.\n- Teide National Park is a national park located in Tenerife in the Canary Islands, Spain.\n- Adenocarpus viscosus can be found above 1800 meters on La Palma in Caldera de Taburiente.\n- Adenocarpus viscosus can be found above 1800 meters on Tenerife, where it is a dominant shrub in Teide National Park.\n- Adenocarpus viscosus also occurs in parts of Corona Forestal Nature Park and Reserva Especial de las Palomas.\n- The chunk mentions Echium wildpretii subsp. trichosiphon, but provides no complete fact about it.",
